"""Friendly situation-led articles with useful, relevant next steps."""
import shutil
from editorial import write_editorial_page

GUIDES=[
 ('surprise-repair-quote','A big repair quote?<br><em>Take the next good step.</em>','A surprise repair quote: what to do next','An expensive recommendation does not have to become an instant decision. Get the finding, understand the choices and compare the same work.','price-notebook.webp','Illustrative project-planning notebook',[
 ('First, get your bearings.','A major quote can make an ordinary afternoon feel very expensive. Before choosing a payment plan or signing an approval, ask what the business found and what the proposed work is intended to solve. If the professional identifies an immediate hazard, ask what precautions are needed; handle safety before shopping.'),
 ('Turn the headline into a scope.','Ask for the equipment or materials, labor, removal, preparation, permits and finishing responsibilities in writing. Which items are included? Which are allowances? What could change once the work begins? A useful quote helps you see the boundaries of the job.'),
 ('Ask about the options.','Could a repair address the immediate problem? Is replacement being recommended for a specific reason? Ask for the expected limitations of each proposed option. Another assessment may be useful when you can safely take time, but confirm whether it has a diagnostic or consultation charge.'),
 ('Compare the job, then the number.','A smaller total can leave out work you need; a larger total may include a different project. Put the scopes side by side. The Wazoozie cost guide gives national planning context, while the comparison tool helps you list the questions that remain. Neither one inspects your home or decides which proposal is right.'),
 ('Leave the conversation with a next step.','You might approve a clearly described repair, request a revised proposal or arrange another assessment. Keep the finding, estimate and written approval together. If the quote is for heating, cooling or hot water, you can discuss a second-opinion visit with Middletown HVAC; other trades have their own local contacts.')],
 'Could you send the finding, the repair and replacement options if applicable, the complete scope, and any charge for a second assessment in writing?',
 [('/compare/','Compare two written estimates'),('/pricing-guide/','Check general cost ranges'),('/start/?intent=secondopinion','Discuss an HVAC second opinion'),('/local-help/','Find the right trade')],
 [('FTC: avoiding home-improvement scams','https://consumer.ftc.gov/articles/how-avoid-home-improvement-scam')]),
 ('one-room-too-hot-too-cold','That one room.<br><em>You know the one.</em>','One room too hot or too cold? Start here','The rest of the house feels fine. One bedroom, addition or home office never quite joins in. Here is how to start a useful comfort conversation.','hvac-comfort.webp','Custom illustration of room-by-room home comfort',[
 ('Describe the room before shopping for a unit.','Is the problem mostly on hot afternoons, cold mornings or whenever the door is closed? Is it a new concern or something the room has always done? Note how you use the space, its windows and any changes to the room or home. You do not need to diagnose it to explain what living there feels like.'),
 ('Ask for an assessment of the cause.','A room’s comfort problem does not identify the right equipment by itself. Ask the professional to assess the space and the existing system rather than choosing solely from square footage or a product photo. Describe any current system fault when arranging the visit so the office can discuss the appropriate appointment.'),
 ('Give ductless a thoughtful look.','DOE describes ductless mini-splits as an option for individual spaces and additions where extending ductwork is difficult. That makes them worth discussing for a stubborn room. It does not establish that every uneven room needs a new system. Ask how the suggested approach compares with addressing the existing system or the room’s other needs.'),
 ('Plan the whole installation.','If ductless looks appropriate, discuss the indoor and outdoor locations, line route, drainage, electrical scope and access for care. Ask how equipment selection accounts for the room and winter conditions. DOE emphasizes that correct sizing and placement matter; the biggest unit is not automatically the best plan.'),
 ('Make the first conversation easy.','Bring your notes, the room’s approximate size and any readily available photos of the space. Middletown HVAC’s ductless planning tool can give a business-specific starting point, followed by a site assessment and written scope. You can also start with the room-comfort service page and decide whether a conversation would be helpful.')],
 'This room feels different when ____. It is used for ____. Could you assess the cause and explain the options, installation scope and visit charge?',
 [('/services/ductless-mini-splits/','Explore room-by-room comfort'),('https://www.mtownhvac.com/ductless-estimator/?utm_source=wazoozie&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=room-guide','Try the ductless planning tool'),('/start/?intent=comfort','Discuss the room with Middletown HVAC')],
 [('DOE: ductless minisplit heat pumps','https://www.energy.gov/energysaver/ductless-minisplit-heat-pumps'),('ENERGY STAR: ductless heating and cooling','https://www.energystar.gov/products/ductless_heating_cooling')]),
 ('car-repair-estimate-changed','The shop called.<br><em>The estimate changed.</em>','Your car-repair estimate changed: what to ask','Additional findings can happen. So can misunderstandings. A calm conversation about the finding, scope and approval keeps the next step clearer.','sound-wraps-project.webp','Vehicle project photo published by Sound Wraps; used as automotive editorial imagery',[
 ('Start with what changed.','Ask the shop to separate the concern you brought in from the additional finding. What was observed? Is there a report, measurement or available photo that would help explain it? A useful explanation should make the recommendation easier to understand without requiring you to become a mechanic.'),
 ('Separate the priorities.','Which work addresses the original concern? Which item has an immediate safety implication, and which is maintenance or an optional improvement? Ask the shop to explain any immediate precautions and whether the vehicle should be driven. This article cannot determine whether your vehicle is safe.'),
 ('Get the revised estimate before approval.','Ask for the added parts and labor, diagnostic charges, taxes and fees, and what the new total includes. Confirm how any previously discussed fee credit works. FTC auto-repair guidance recommends arranging approval before the shop exceeds an agreed amount.'),
 ('A second opinion can be a good question.','For a costly or complicated repair, the FTC suggests considering another opinion. Before moving the vehicle, ask about the diagnostic bill, any reassembly or storage terms, and safe transport. Another shop may need to perform its own assessment; a phone description is not a diagnosis.'),
 ('Keep the paper trail.','Save the original estimate, revised scope, your approval and the final invoice. Ask for written warranty terms. If an item on the bill is unclear, ask for its purpose, price and approval record. When you need a local introduction, Wazoozie lists general repair shops and a separate transmission specialist so you can start the right conversation.')],
 'What changed from the first estimate, which items are urgent or optional, what is the revised total, and will you get my approval before additional work?',
 [('/auto-mechanics/','Explore local auto-repair contacts'),('/businesses/trans-man-transmissions-eddystone/','Discuss a transmission concern'),('/before-you-say-yes/#auto-repair','Bring the auto-repair questions')],
 [('FTC: auto-repair basics','https://consumer.ftc.gov/articles/0211-auto-repair-basics')]),
]


def add(out,origin,pages):
    import html
    e=html.escape
    for slug,headline,title,lede,photo,alt,sections,question,links,sources in GUIDES:
        body='<article class="wrap situation-article"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/home-tips/">The field guide</a><span>/</span>What to do next</div><div class="situation-cover"><div><div class="eyebrow">THE NEXT GOOD STEP · WAZOOZIE</div><h1>'+headline+'</h1><p>'+e(lede)+'</p><span class="situation-date">Checked November 6, 2026 · Practical planning guidance</span></div><figure><img src="/assets/'+photo+'" alt="'+e(alt)+'" width="960" height="640"><figcaption>'+('Photo: Sound Wraps LLC · <a href="https://www.facebook.com/photo/?fbid=1575250094402346">Original public photo ↗</a>. The photo illustrates automotive work; it does not document the repair scenario in this article.' if photo=='sound-wraps-project.webp' else 'Custom Wazoozie editorial illustration; not a documented customer project.')+'</figcaption></figure></div><div class="situation-content">'
        for heading,copy in sections:body+='<section><h2>'+e(heading)+'</h2><p>'+e(copy)+'</p></section>'
        body+='<aside class="situation-script"><div class="eyebrow">BORROW THIS FIRST LINE</div><p data-situation-question>'+e(question)+'</p><button class="btn outline" type="button" data-copy-situation hidden>Copy these questions</button><p class="situation-copy-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><textarea class="situation-copy-text" aria-label="Questions to copy" readonly hidden></textarea></aside><section class="situation-next"><h2>Your next good step.</h2><div>'+''.join('<a class="btn '+('primary' if i==0 else 'outline')+'" href="'+e(url,quote=True)+'">'+e(label)+' →</a>' for i,(url,label) in enumerate(links))+'</div></section><section class="situation-sources"><h2>Sources & context.</h2><p>Wazoozie’s practical editorial guidance draws on the sources below. It is not a diagnosis, a safety clearance or a quote. Wazoozie is operated by Bryan Cordy, owner of Middletown HVAC; HVAC contact and estimator links are referrals to that business. Choose the business and agree on the work directly.</p><ul>'+''.join('<li><a href="'+url+'">'+e(label)+' ↗</a></li>' for label,url in sources)+'</ul></section></div></article>'
        write_editorial_page(out,origin,pages,'/guides/'+slug+'/',title,lede,body)
        target=out/'guides'/slug/'index.html';s=target.read_text().replace('</head>','<link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/situation-guides.css"></head>').replace('</body>','<script type="module" src="/assets/situation-guides.js"></script></body>');target.write_text(s)
    cards='<section class="wrap situation-new" aria-labelledby="situation-new-title"><div class="eyebrow">LIFE HAS QUESTIONS. START HERE.</div><h2 id="situation-new-title">What do I do now?</h2><div>'+''.join('<a href="/guides/'+slug+'/"><span>THE NEXT GOOD STEP</span><h3>'+e(title)+'</h3><p>'+e(lede)+'</p><strong>Read the friendly field guide →</strong></a>' for slug,headline,title,lede,*_ in GUIDES)+'</div></section>'
    for path,marker in [(out/'index.html','<section class="wrap journal-home"'),(out/'home-tips/index.html','</main>'),(out/'guides/index.html','</main>')]:
        s=path.read_text().replace(marker,cards+marker,1).replace('</head>','<link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/situation-guides.css"></head>',1);path.write_text(s)
    for asset in ('situation-guides.css','situation-guides.js'):shutil.copy(out.parent/'assets'/asset,out/'assets'/asset)
